# Thread status

Maintain exactly one leading status emoji and a space in the current chat's title, preserving its existing title body. Use a supported native current-chat rename capability; the optional thread-status hook provides client identity and a Claude SDK helper. Check available capabilities once, without repeatedly searching for missing tools. Never edit client databases or handcraft transcript records. If the surface cannot rename, report that limit once and continue; a proposed title is not an applied change.

Use 🔄 working; 🙋 required user input, decision or permission; ⏳ an external event already underway; 🚧 a blocker requiring action; 👀 required review/acceptance; ⏸️ explicitly paused; 🏁 ready to close (requested work and required checks complete, no required steps remain); ✅ explicitly closed or confirmed archived; ❔ insufficient evidence. Idle, a completed response, session exit and age do not establish completion. Optional suggestions do not keep a completed task open. A new work request reopens it; a status question alone does not. Preserve explicit pauses until resumed.

Update on meaningful transitions, including before required user input and before the final log_interaction. Replace existing recognized prefixes rather than accumulating them; preserve unrelated decorative emoji. Use only the known current chat, never guess IDs, bulk-rename other chats or message them to request a change. Subagents must not rename their parent's chat. Renaming or marking ✅ does not itself archive anything; archiving still follows the user's request.
